property_value: x_1.1:description "The ontology for the Anatomy of the Insect SkeletoMuscular system (AISM) contains terms used to describe the cuticle - as a single anatomical structure - and the skeletal muscle system, to be used in insect biodiversity research." xsd:string
property_value: x_1.1:title "Ontology for the Anatomy of the Insect SkeletoMuscular system" xsd:string

[Term]
id: AISM:0000000
name: cuticular internal depression
def: "The projection of the inner surface of the cuticle." [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-05-19"}
is_a: AISM:0000174 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect region of cuticle
relationship: BFO:0000050 BSPO:0000061 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! part of proximal side
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0001857 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! has characteristic concave

[Term]
id: AISM:0000001
name: resilin {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"}
def: "Resilin is an elastomeric protein found in many insects and other arthropods. It provides soft rubber-elasticity to mechanically active organs and tissue.\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resilin" [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"}
is_a: PR:000000001 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"} ! protein
property_value: IAO:0000232 "This is a generalized term to refer to this protein as the only option available now is pro-resilin (fruit fly) [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_Q9V7U0]" xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000002
name: insect articulation
def: "The region of cuticle that is composed two articular surfaces that are adjacent to each other." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
is_a: AISM:0000174 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect region of cuticle
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Articulations are 'anatomical clusters', collections of not direclty connected (continuous) sclerite surfaces that are adjacent to another sclerite. The cranio-mandibular articulation is the articular surface of the cranium and the adjacent articular surface of the mandible. The articular surfaces are sometimes located on the same sclerite." xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000003
name: insect sclerite {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Sclerite: distinctly sclerotized region of the integument, with thick layer of exocuticle.\"", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-01-09: specifying insect sclerite.\njgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
def: "The region of the insect cuticle that is less flexible than the neighboring conjunctiva(e) (conjunctiva(e) that the sclerite is continuous with." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
xref: http://flybase.org/cgi-bin/fbcvq.html?query=FBbt\:00004475 "sclerite"
xref: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HAO_0000909 "sclerite" {def="The area of the cuticle that is less flexible than adjacent conjunctivae."}
xref: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_6004475 "insect sclerite"
is_a: AISM:0000174 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect region of cuticle
property_value: IAO:0000118 "esclerito" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-01-09"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000004
name: conjunctiva
def: "The region of the insect cuticle that is more flexible than the neighboring sclerite(s) [sclerite(s) that the conjunctiva is continuous with]." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
synonym: "membrane" EXACT [] {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Membrane: very flexible, unsclerotized area of the integument.\""}
xref: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HAO_0000221 "conjunctiva" {def="The area of the cuticle that is more flexible than adjacent sclerites."}
is_a: AISM:0000174 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect region of cuticle
relationship: RO:0002150 AISM:0000003 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! continuous with insect sclerite
property_value: IAO:0000232 "Conjunctivae are more flexible and usually less thick than sclerties of the cuticle allowing the sclerites to move relative to each other.\nMicro-CT based methods cannot be used to accurately differentiate slcerites from conjunctiuvae. CLSM (the excitation wavelengths of sclerites and conjunctivae are different in response of 488 nm emission vawelength), histological sections or simple dissections need to be applied to define relative flexibility of the insect cuticle.\n\nIf a conjunctiva entirelly encircles a sclerite, then the 'encircles' and 'encircled by' object properties are used to link the sclerite and the conjunctiva even in cases in which the encircled sclerites or conjunctivae are part of an evagination allowing to model spatial relationship between appendage segments: the pedicel is encircled by the scapal-pedicellar conjunctiva, which is encircled by the scape or the the coxa encircles the coxo-femoral conjunctiuva that encircels the femur." xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000005
name: cuticular depression
def: "The region of the cuticle that corresponds to a concave surface." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
is_a: BFO:0000004 ! independent continuant
relationship: BSPO:0000125 AISM:0000174 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! in distal side of insect region of cuticle
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0001857 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! has characteristic concave
property_value: IAO:0000232 "External cuticular depression. The surface of the cuticle in insects is the entire surface of an organism, and it is composed of flat, concave and convex regions. Concavities sometimes correspons with invaginations of the cuticle and the underlaying sinlge layer epidermis, somtimes correspond to a decreased cuticular thickness." xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000006
name: cuticular invagination
def: "The region of cuticle that corresponds with an invagination of the single layer epidermis (epidermal fold). The cuticular invagination sometimes corresponds to a cuticular depression (concavity on the surface of the cuticle)." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
is_a: AISM:0000174 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect region of cuticle
relationship: RO:0002008 AISM:0000000 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! coincident with cuticular internal depression
relationship: RO:0002008 AISM:0000005 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! coincident with cuticular depression

[Term]
id: AISM:0000007
name: elastic cuticle {creation_date="2020-10-27"}
def: "The region of cuticle with higher content of resilin." [] {creation_date="2021-04-21", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
is_a: AISM:0000174 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect region of cuticle
is_a: PR:000050567 ! protein-containing material entity
relationship: RO:0002473 AISM:0000001 {IAO:0000232="Modified 2024-02-14: updated to 'composed primarily of' and linked to resilin\njgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! composed primarily of resilin

[Term]
id: AISM:0000008
name: cuticular protrusion
def: "The region of the cuticle that corresponds to a convex surface." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
is_a: AISM:0000174 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect region of cuticle
relationship: BFO:0000050 BSPO:0000062 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! part of distal side
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0001355 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! has characteristic convex
property_value: IAO:0000232 "The surface of the cuticle in insects is the entire surface of an organism, and it is composed of flat, concave and convex regions. Convexities sometimes correspons with evaginations of the cuticle and the underlaying sinlge layer epidermis and sometimes correspond to an increased cuticular thickness.\"" xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000009
name: cuticular fossa {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"}
def: "The cuticular depression that is adjacent to a cuticular condyle." [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"}
is_a: AISM:0000005 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"} ! cuticular depression
relationship: RO:0002220 AISM:0000010 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"} ! adjacent to cuticular condyle

[Term]
id: AISM:0000010
name: cuticular condyle {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"}
def: "The cuticular protrusion that is part of an insect sclerite and adjacent to an articular surface." [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"}
is_a: AISM:0000008 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"} ! cuticular protrusion
relationship: BFO:0000050 AISM:0000003 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"} ! part of insect sclerite
relationship: RO:0002220 AISM:0000167 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"} ! adjacent to articular surface

[Term]
id: AISM:0000013
name: evaginated {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
def: "A part or structure that is produced by evagination." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2021-04-21"}
is_a: PATO:0001355 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! convex

[Term]
id: AISM:0000014
name: insect cranio-mandibular articulation {IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-02-05: specified insect.\njgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
def: "The articulation between the mandible and the cranium." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
is_a: AISM:0000002 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect articulation

[Term]
id: AISM:0000015
name: cranio-cardinal articulation
def: "The articulation between the cardo and the head capsule." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
is_a: AISM:0000002 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect articulation

[Term]
id: AISM:0000016
name: cranio-antennal articulation
def: "The articulation between the scapus and the cranium." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
is_a: AISM:0000002 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect articulation

[Term]
id: AISM:0000017
name: insect head-cervical articulation {IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-02-05: specified insect.\njgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
def: "The articulation between the head and the neck." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-10-27"}
is_a: AISM:0000002 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect articulation

[Term]
id: AISM:0000018
name: cardo {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter. \n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Cardo: basal element of maxilla, articulating with head capsule; usually moved by one cranial muscle and one tentorial muscle.\"", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The sclerite of the insect maxilla that is attached to the head capsule by the oral foraminal conjunctiva and to the cuticle of stipes by the stipito-cardinal conjunctiva." [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
is_a: AISM:0000003 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect sclerite
relationship: BFO:0000050 AISM:0000044 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! part of insect maxilla
relationship: RO:0002150 AISM:0000099 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! continuous with oral foraminal conjunctiva
relationship: RO:0002150 AISM:0000110 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! continuous with cardo-stipital conjunctiva
relationship: RO:0002220 AISM:0000019 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! adjacent to head capsule
relationship: RO:0002220 AISM:0000111 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! adjacent to stipes
property_value: IAO:0000589 "cuticle of cardo" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-04-13"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000019
name: head capsule {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"The head capsule is almost always a rigid, well sclerotized structural unit, equipped with a defined set of appendages. It is reinforced by strengthening ridges and the endoskeletal tentorium\""}
def: "The sclerite of the insect head that is attached to the neck membrane and the oral foraminal conjunctiva, bears the eye cuticle and surrounds the brain" [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
synonym: "cephalic capsule" EXACT [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
synonym: "insect cranium" EXACT [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}
is_a: AISM:0000003 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect sclerite
relationship: AISM:0000078 AISM:0000099 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! encircles oral foraminal conjunctiva
relationship: BFO:0000050 AISM:0000107 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! part of insect head
relationship: BFO:0000051 AISM:0000088 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! has part eye cuticle
relationship: RO:0002150 AISM:0000098 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! continuous with neck membrane
relationship: RO:0002221 UBERON:0000955 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! surrounds brain

[Term]
id: AISM:0000020
name: dorsal second axillary sclerite
def: "The axillary sclerite that is on the dorsal region of the basal wing conjunctiva and lateral to the first axillary sclerite." [] {creation_date="2021-04-10", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
is_a: AISM:0004161 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! axillary sclerite
relationship: AISM:0000011 AISM:0000022 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! lateral_to first axillary sclerite

[Term]
id: AISM:0000021
name: abdominal tergite I
def: "Is the abdominal tergite of the preabdomen that is attached to the posterior margin of the tergum by the metanoto-abdominal tergite I conjunctiva." [] {IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed distally adjacent elements to avoid problems with their absence during presence/absence reasoning.\njgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-03-18"}
is_a: AISM:0004057 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! abdominal tergite
relationship: anteriorly_connected_to AISM:0004082 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! metanoto-abdominal tergite I conjunctiva
relationship: BFO:0000050 AISM:0004055 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! part of preabdomen

[Term]
id: AISM:0000022
name: first axillary sclerite
def: "The axillary sclerite that is part of the dorsal region of the basal wing conjunctiva and is anterior to the third axillary sclerite." [] {creation_date="2021-04-10", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
is_a: AISM:0004161 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! axillary sclerite
relationship: BSPO:0000096 AISM:0004223 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! anterior to third axillary sclerite

[Term]
id: AISM:0000023
name: galea {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Galea: outer endite lobe of maxilla, usually semimembranous and equipped with sensilla (mainly chemoreceptors).\"", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The cuticle of the appendage of the insect maxilla that is attached to the stipes by the stipito-galeal conjunctiva." [] {term:modified="2021-12-08", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
is_a: AISM:0000029 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! insect appendage
relationship: BFO:0000050 AISM:0000044 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! part of insect maxilla
relationship: RO:0002150 AISM:0004011 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! continuous with stipito-galeal conjunctiva
relationship: RO:0002220 AISM:0000111 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! adjacent to stipes
property_value: IAO:0000589 "cuticle of galea" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-04-13"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000024
name: labial palpus {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Labial palp: tactile appendage of the labium.\"", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The cuticle of the paired appendage of the labium that is attached to the palpiger by the palpigero-palpal conjunctiva." [] {term:modified="2021-12-08", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
is_a: AISM:0000029 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect appendage
relationship: AISM:0000079 AISM:0004017 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! encircled by palpigero-palpal conjunctiva
relationship: BFO:0000050 AISM:0000087 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! part of labium
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0040024 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! has characteristic bilaterally paired
relationship: RO:0002220 AISM:0004006 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! adjacent to palpiger
property_value: IAO:0000589 "cuticle of labial palpus" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-04-13"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000026
name: lacinia {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Lacinia: inner endite lobe of maxilla, usually firmly connected or fused with stipes; usually sclerotized, with mesally curved apex and articulated spines arranged along mesal edge.\"", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The cuticle of the appendage of the insect maxilla that is attached to the cuticle of stipes by the stipito-lacinial conjunctiva." [] {term:modified="2021-12-08", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
is_a: AISM:0000029 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! insect appendage
relationship: BFO:0000050 AISM:0000044 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! part of insect maxilla
relationship: RO:0002150 AISM:0004009 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! continuous with stipito-lacinial conjunctiva
relationship: RO:0002220 AISM:0000111 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! adjacent to stipes
property_value: IAO:0000589 "cuticle of lacinia" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-04-13"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000027
name: cuticular evagination
def: "The region of cuticle that corresponds with an evagination of the cuticle and the single layer epidermis (epidermal fold). The cuticular evagination usually corresponds to a cuticular protrusion (convexity on the surface of the cuticle)." [] {creation_date="2020-11-11", x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}
is_a: AISM:0000008 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! cuticular protrusion
intersection_of: AISM:0000008 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-08-01"} ! cuticular protrusion
intersection_of: RO:0000053 AISM:0000013 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-08-01"} ! has characteristic evaginated
intersection_of: RO:0002008 UBERON:0005157 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-08-01"} ! coincident with epithelial fold
relationship: RO:0000053 AISM:0000013 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! has characteristic evaginated
relationship: RO:0002008 UBERON:0005157 {creation_date="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! coincident with epithelial fold

[Term]
id: AISM:0000028
name: solid cuticular protrusion {creation_date="2020-11-11"}
def: "The cuticular protrusion that does not correspond to an evagination." [] {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2021-04-21"}
is_a: AISM:0000008 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! cuticular protrusion

[Term]
id: AISM:0000029
name: insect appendage {AISM:0000171="Nichols, S. W. (1989) Torre-Bueno glossary of entomology. New York Entomological Society. 840 pp.\n\nhttps://ipmhouse.tamu.edu/files/2021/03/The-Torre-Bueno-Glossary-of-Entomology.pdf\n\n\"any part, piece, or organ attached by a joint to the body or to any other main structure\"", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The evagination of the cuticle that is musculated (connected to the body via muscles)." [] {creation_date="2020-11-11", x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}
is_a: AISM:0000128 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! multicellular cuticular evagination
intersection_of: AISM:0000128 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-08-01"} ! multicellular cuticular evagination
intersection_of: RO:0002150 UBERON:0014895 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-08-01"} ! continuous with somatic muscle, invertebrate
relationship: RO:0002150 UBERON:0014895 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! continuous with somatic muscle, invertebrate
property_value: IAO:0000589 "cuticle of insect appendage" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-04-13"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000031
