[Term]
id: AISM:0000039
name: cuticular seta {creation_date="2020-11-11", AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Seta (=macrotrichium): articulated hair with socket, formed by trichogen cell.\"", term:modified="2021-12-10"}
def: "The unicellular cuticular evagination that constitutes a sclerite with its base surrounded by socket membrane." [] {creation_date="2021-04-21", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
is_a: AISM:0000003 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect sclerite
is_a: AISM:0000127 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! unicellular cuticular evagination
relationship: AISM:0000079 AISM:0000102 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! encircled by ring conjunctiva

[Term]
id: AISM:0000040
name: cuticular spur {source="https://doi.org/10.1016/0020-7322(79)90013-8", AISM:0000171="Richards AG, Richards PA (1979) The cuticular protuberances of insects. International Journal of Insect Morphology and Embryology 8: 143–157. \n\n\"Multicellular protuberances without differentiation of specialized cells\"", term:modified="2021-12-10"}
def: "The multicellular evagination of the cuticle that corresponds to an epithelial fold, composed of some sclerite that is encricled by a conjunctiva (moveable)." [] {creation_date="2020-11-11", x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}
is_a: AISM:0000003 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect sclerite
is_a: AISM:0000128 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! multicellular cuticular evagination
relationship: AISM:0000079 AISM:0000102 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! encircled by ring conjunctiva
property_value: IAO:0000232 "The difference between an appendage and a spur is the lack of muscles attached to the spur, otherwise, the mandible would be also a spur. Spines are multicellular evaginations that are not encircled by conjunctivae. Moveable beetle horns are spurs while not moveable beetle horns are spines." xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-11-11"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000041
name: cuticular scale {term:modified="2021-12-10"}
def: "The seta that is flat." [] {creation_date="2020-11-11", x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}
is_a: AISM:0000039 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! cuticular seta
relationship: RO:0000053 PATO:0002254 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! has characteristic flattened

[Term]
id: AISM:0000042
name: labrum {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Labrum: unpaired upper lip, connected with distal edge of clypeus.\"", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The cuticle of the mouthpart and appendage that is attached to the clypeus by the clypeo-labral conjunctiva and to the proximal margin of the epipharynx." [] {term:modified="2021-12-08", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
is_a: AISM:0000165 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! mouthpart
relationship: RO:0002150 AISM:0004018 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! continuous with clypeo-labral conjunctiva
relationship: RO:0002220 AISM:0004019 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! adjacent to clypeus
property_value: IAO:0000589 "cuticle of labrum" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-04-13"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000043
name: insect mandible {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter. \n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"The mandibles are the paired appendages of the 4th head segment and receive their innervation from the anterior part of the suboesophageal ganglion [...] They are primarily a compact, undivided and strongly sclerotized element without appendages.\"", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The cuticle of the mouthpart and sclerite between the cuticle of the labrum and the cuticle of the insect maxilla that is attached to the head capsule by the oral foraminal conjunctiva and the cranio-mandibular muscle." [] {term:modified="2021-12-08", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
is_a: AISM:0000003 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! insect sclerite
