[Term]
id: AISM:0000090
name: cuticular tendon {AISM:0000171="Klass K-D (2001) The female abdomen of the viviparous earwig Hemimerus vosseleri (Insecta: Dermaptera: Hemimeridae), with a discussion of the postgenital abdomen of Insecta. Zoological Journal of the Linnean Society 131: 251–307. \n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1111/j.1096-3642.2001.tb02239.x \n\n\"tendon is used herein to designate membranous internal cuticular projections\""}
def: "The apodeme of elastic cuticle that is continuous with somatic muscle." [] {x_1.1:contributor="2022-06-22", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
