id: AISM:0000098
name: neck membrane
def: "The conjuctiva that is continuous with the posterior margin of the head capsule and with the anterior margin of the prothorax, and bears cervical sclerites." [] {creation_date="2020-11-11", x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", term:modified="2022-06-27"}
synonym: "cervical membrane" EXACT [] {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Cervical membrane: membrane connecting the head and prothorax.\""}
is_a: AISM:0000004 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! conjunctiva
