relationship: BFO:0000051 AISM:0004126 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! has part mesothorax
relationship: BFO:0000051 AISM:0004127 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! has part metathorax
relationship: BSPO:0000096 AISM:0000109 {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"} ! anterior to insect abdomen
relationship: BSPO:0000099 AISM:0000098 {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"} ! posterior to neck membrane
property_value: IAO:0000232 "The hind leg muscles sometimes attach to the second abdominal sternite. The abdominal sopiracles are different in their structure from tghe thoracic spiracles as they are opened and closed by two articulating sclerites that are moved by two sets of muscles whereas the thoracic spiracles are closed by only one occlusor muscle and opened by the flexibility of the distal tracheal region. The border between the thorax and the abdomen is sometimes marked by the anterior first abdmonial tergal conjunctiva. In Hymenoptera, the border between the abdomen and the thorax cannot be defined as the anterior first abdmonial tergal conjunctiva is absent, the sclerite that receives muscles from the metacoxa also contains the first abdominal spiracle." xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075", creation_date="2020-11-11"}
property_value: IAO:0000589 "cuticle of insect thorax" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-04-13"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000109
name: insect abdomen {IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The region of the cuticle that is an insect tagmatic subdivision of the integument, posterior to the thorax." [] {creation_date="2020-11-11", IAO:0000232="Modified 2024-01-25: added 'insect tagmatic subdivision of integument'.\njgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", x_1.1:contributor="imiko https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2938-9075"}
