[Term]
id: AISM:0000159
name: salivarium {def="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Salivarium: posterior part of preoral space between hypopharynx and labium, with opening of salivary ducts.\""}
def: "The conjunctiva in the head capsule that forms a pouch between the hypopharynx and the labium and bears the exocrine gland duct." [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
