property_value: IAO:0000232 "Edited by jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883 \n2024-05-11\nTo make it a distance as opposed to an anatomical space and change 'adjacent to' for 'characteristic of'\nMatching existing definitions e.g. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/AGRO_00000318\n\nFormer definition based on suggestions at https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/3188" xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2024-02-14"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000377
name: proximal carina of tergite VIII {creation_date="2023-06-04", IAO:0000232="Moved from COLAO to AISM: 2023-05-08\ngmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364", x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364"}
def: "The cuticular carina that is located on the proximal margin of the 8th tergite and is parallel to the left-right body axis." [] {creation_date="2023-06-04", x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364"}
synonym: "pygidium basal ridge" EXACT [] {creation_date="2023-06-04", AISM:0000171="Tarasov, S. I., & Solodovnikov, A. Y. (2011). Phylogenetic analyses reveal reliable morphological markers to classify mega‐diversity in Onthophagini dung beetles (Coleoptera: Scarabaeidae: Scarabaeinae). Cladistics, 27(5), 490-528. https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1096-0031.2011.00351.x\n \nPage 526, character 30", x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364"}
is_a: AISM:0000180 {x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364", creation_date="2023-06-04"} ! tergal carina
relationship: parallel_to BSPO:0000017 {x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364", creation_date="2023-06-04"} ! left-right axis
property_value: IAO:0000232 "In Scarabaeinae, this carina (when present) is located in the proximalmost margin of the surface of the 8th tergite (pygidium) that is not covered by elytra." xsd:string {x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364", creation_date="2023-06-04"}

[Term]
id: AISM:0000378
name: granulate cuticular puncture {creation_date="2023-06-04", AISM:0000171="Orbigny, H. d’ (1913) [1913-1914]. Synopsis des Onthophagides d’Afrique. Annales de la Société entomologique de France, 82 : 1-742.\nhttps://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/page/8239919\n\n\"la ponctuation peut être râpeuse ou granuleuse, c'est-à-dire composée de points dont le bord antérieur s'élève en une aspérité irrégulière, ou en un granule arrondi qui ordinaireauent échancre plus ou moins ce bord antérieur\" p. 4", IAO:0000232="Moved from COLAO to AISM: 2023-05-08\ngmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364", x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364"}
def: "The cuticular puncture that has a cuticular granule on its anterior margin." [] {creation_date="2023-06-04", x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364"}
is_a: AISM:0000524 {x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364", creation_date="2023-06-04"} ! cuticular puncture

[Term]
id: AISM:0000379
name: ocellate cuticular puncture {creation_date="2023-06-04", AISM:0000171="Orbigny, H. d’ (1913) [1913-1914]. Synopsis des Onthophagides d’Afrique. Annales de la Société entomologique de France, 82 : 1-742.\n\nhttps://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/page/8239919\n\n\"... soit grands et à fond plat, ou ocellés, c'est-à-dire grands et à fond convexe, ou ombiliqués, c'est-à-dire grands, peu profonds et ayant dans l'intérieur un petit point plus profond\" p. 4", IAO:0000232="Moved from COLAO to AISM: 2023-05-08\ngmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364", x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364"}
def: "The cuticular puncture that is flattened." [] {creation_date="2023-06-04", x_1.1:contributor="gmontanaro https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0836-1364"}

[Term]
