[Term]
id: AISM:0004019
name: clypeus {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Clypeus: anteroventral part of head capsule; primarily separated from frons by transverse frontoclypeal strengthening ridge between anterior tentorial pits; usually bearing the labrum at its distal margin.\""}
def: "The region of the head capsule that is anterior to the frons and is attached to the labrum by the clypeo-labral conjunctiva" [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-02-19"}
