[Term]
id: AISM:0004039
name: dorsal tentorial arm {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Dorsal tentorial arm: paired dorsal element of tentorium, originating at anterior arm or connecting area of anterior and posterior arm; often connected with head capsule by fibrillae.\""}
def: "The apophysis of the tentorium that is connected to an anterior tentorial arm." [] {creation_date="2021-02-24", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
