[Term]
id: AISM:0004054
name: laminatentoria {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"In some groups an accessory bridge is formed by medially fused internally directed processes, the laminatentoria. This feature is sometimes erroneously referred to as “perforated corpotentorium”.\""}
def: "Are apophyses of the tentorium originating at each anterior tentorial arm." [] {creation_date="2021-02-24", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
