[Term]
id: AISM:0004151
name: epipleurite {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Epipleurites: basalare and subalare.\""}
def: "The sclerite of the insect thorax that is surrounded by the noto-pleural conjunctiva and is adjacent to the wing." [] {x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2021-04-05"}
