[Term]
id: AISM:0004246
name: anal vein of the insect wing {IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-01-09: specifying insect wing vein.\njgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Anal veins: longitudinal veins of the anal field proximally articulated with 3rd axillary sclerite; usually unbranched and arranged like a fan.\""}
def: "The insect wing vein of the anal field that is posterior to the anal fold or the postcubitus and anterior to the jugal fold or the jugal veins." [] {creation_date="2021-09-07", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883"}
