id: AISM:0004309
name: arolium {AISM:0000171="Beutel RG, Friedrich F, Yang X-K, Ge S-Q (2014) Insect Morphology and Phylogeny Insect morphology and phylogeny: a textbook for students of entomology. De Gruyter.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1515/9783110264043\n\n\"Arolium: the median hollow lobe of the pretarsus. It can be completely membranous or partly sclerotized.\" p. 42.\n\"unpaired, between the claws\" p. 40.", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2023-01-11", IAO:0000232="Modified 2023-04-13: removed ‘cuticle of’ from label.\nstarasov https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5237-2330"}
def: "The medial cuticular protrusion of the distitarsus." [] {IAO:0000232="Modified 2026-02-14: Updated to distitarsus.\njgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", x_1.1:contributor="jgiron https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0851-6883", creation_date="2023-01-11"}
property_value: IAO:0000589 "cuticle of arolium" xsd:string {creation_date="2023-04-13"}

