[Term]
id: UBERON:0001173
name: biliary tree
namespace: uberon
def: "A complex network of conduits that begins with the canals of Hering (intralobar bile duct) and progressively merges into a system of interlobular, septal, and major ducts which then coalesce to form the extrahepatic bile ducts, which finally deliver bile to the intestine, and in some species to the gallbladder." [DOI:10.1002/ar.20664]
